<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kebineng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 235</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kebineng (died 235) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> chieftain who rebuilt a large confederation on the northern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after the break-up of Tanshihuai's realm. Aided by Chinese refugees, he adopted Chinese-style weapons, armour and organisation, and by the 220s controlled lands from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-river">Liao River</a> westwards. Rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> grew, and in 235 an assassin sent by the Wei inspector Wang Xiong killed him, after which his confederation broke up.</p></div>
